  "changelog": "Initial release of psychiatry-pmph-9edition\n\n- Provides 47 core clinical skills based on the 9th edition of People's Medical Publishing House's Psychiatry.\n- Covers clinical assessment, diagnostic classification, pharmacologic and psychological treatment, emergency intervention, forensic evaluation, and community rehabilitation.\n- Structured, evidence-based clinical decision support for psychiatrists and mental health professionals.\n- Includes detailed subskills across areas such as mood, anxiety, psychosis, neurocognitive, eating, sleep, substance use, personality, trauma-related, emergency, forensic, and rehabilitation disorders.\n- Chinese-language documentation and structured usage examples for integration with ClawHub-enabled assistants.",
